WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.001
Russian President Vladimir

00:00:01.001 --> 00:00:02.435
Putin today making it official.

00:00:02.435 --> 00:00:03.803
He just formally suspended

00:00:03.803 --> 00:00:04.771
Russia's involvement

00:00:04.771 --> 00:00:06.573
in its last remaining nuclear arms

00:00:06.573 --> 00:00:08.174
control treaty with the United States.

00:00:08.174 --> 00:00:09.042
That move

00:00:09.042 --> 00:00:11.211
coming after a rare admission

00:00:11.211 --> 00:00:12.278
from President Putin

00:00:12.278 --> 00:00:13.680
about losses on the battlefield

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:14.714
in Ukraine

00:00:15.815 --> 00:00:16.783
and pneumonia.

00:00:16.783 --> 00:00:17.684
Unfortunately,

00:00:17.684 --> 00:00:19.352
there are losses in our ranks

00:00:19.352 --> 00:00:20.754
the leadership of the FSB

00:00:20.754 --> 00:00:22.288
must do everything to provide

00:00:22.288 --> 00:00:23.189
additional support

00:00:23.189 --> 00:00:25.291
to the families of our fallen comrades.

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:27.994
On that battlefield today,

00:00:27.994 --> 00:00:29.763
the eastern city of Bermuda

00:00:29.763 --> 00:00:31.398
is a flash point as it is the landscape

00:00:31.398 --> 00:00:33.233
calling the battle, quote, challenging.

00:00:33.233 --> 00:00:34.167
Ukrainian soldiers

00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:36.002
paint a much more dire picture to CNN,

00:00:36.002 --> 00:00:37.003
saying the situation

00:00:37.003 --> 00:00:37.837
is, quote,

00:00:37.837 --> 00:00:40.807
100% worse than what's being reported.

00:00:41.174 --> 00:00:41.975
And as Melissa Bell

00:00:41.975 --> 00:00:43.109
is live for us on the ground

00:00:43.109 --> 00:00:44.344
in the Ukrainian capital of Kiev,

00:00:44.344 --> 00:00:45.278
Melissa, what's the latest

00:00:47.881 --> 00:00:49.049
Well, hellish is

00:00:49.049 --> 00:00:49.382
the way

00:00:49.382 --> 00:00:51.151
another Ukrainian soldier described it

00:00:51.151 --> 00:00:52.185
to CNN.

00:00:52.185 --> 00:00:53.553
John, the picture they paint

00:00:53.553 --> 00:00:54.521
is really pretty horrendous.

00:00:54.521 --> 00:00:55.622
What you're talking about is a town

00:00:55.622 --> 00:00:56.856
that's been the subject of fighting

00:00:56.856 --> 00:00:58.158
for so many weeks now.

00:00:58.158 --> 00:00:58.958
The conditions

00:00:58.958 --> 00:01:00.126
there have worsened as

00:01:00.126 --> 00:01:01.094
the ground has thawed.

00:01:01.094 --> 00:01:02.529
There's flooding in some areas,

00:01:02.529 --> 00:01:04.531
impassable roads and others.

00:01:04.531 --> 00:01:05.598
But those Ukrainian soldiers

00:01:05.598 --> 00:01:05.765
that are

00:01:05.765 --> 00:01:07.033
saying, look, we're holding firm

00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:08.101
despite Russian claims,

00:01:08.101 --> 00:01:09.536
they say Russian forces,

00:01:09.536 --> 00:01:10.804
even though they've been sending

00:01:10.804 --> 00:01:12.672
their most battle-hardened regular

00:01:12.672 --> 00:01:13.773
but also

00:01:13.773 --> 00:01:14.808
volunteer mercenaries

00:01:14.808 --> 00:01:15.508
to try and break

00:01:15.508 --> 00:01:17.110
through Ukrainian defenses

00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:17.911
The Ukrainian soldiers

00:01:17.911 --> 00:01:18.378
saying

00:01:18.378 --> 00:01:20.213
they simply have not encircled us yet

00:01:20.213 --> 00:01:21.915
and that there are still two roads

00:01:21.915 --> 00:01:22.849
through which they continue

00:01:22.849 --> 00:01:24.250
to get their much needed supplies,

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:24.818
even though they're

00:01:24.818 --> 00:01:26.019
coming under enemy fire.

00:01:26.019 --> 00:01:27.954
But really a very grim picture

00:01:27.954 --> 00:01:29.089
being painted about

00:01:29.089 --> 00:01:31.591
what those Ukrainian forces are facing

00:01:31.591 --> 00:01:32.959
as they try and hold firm now.

00:01:32.959 --> 00:01:33.593
For several days

00:01:33.593 --> 00:01:34.661
now, we've been hearing

00:01:34.661 --> 00:01:37.297
growingly desperate pleas for more

00:01:37.764 --> 00:01:38.965
allied equipment

00:01:38.965 --> 00:01:41.167
and help in the shape of F-16s.

00:01:41.201 --> 00:01:41.601
Now, of course,

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:43.303
Washington's ruled those out.

00:01:43.303 --> 00:01:44.370
But we do know that

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:46.539
there is other weaponry coming online

00:01:46.539 --> 00:01:47.373
fairly quickly.

00:01:47.373 --> 00:01:48.208
We've just been hearing

00:01:48.208 --> 00:01:49.209
from an American official

00:01:49.209 --> 00:01:50.543
speaking to the Armed Services

00:01:50.543 --> 00:01:51.511
Committee, saying

00:01:51.511 --> 00:01:54.414
that it is some 4000 Ukrainian soldiers

00:01:54.414 --> 00:01:55.115
that are now being trained,

00:01:55.115 --> 00:01:56.182
not just the United States.

00:01:56.182 --> 00:01:57.884
But in Europe, across Europe,

00:01:57.884 --> 00:01:59.319
on the Patriot systems,

00:01:59.319 --> 00:02:00.820
for instance, on the leopard tanks.

00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:01.187
And, of course,

00:02:01.187 --> 00:02:02.822
those are expected to make

00:02:02.822 --> 00:02:03.823
a big difference.

00:02:03.823 --> 00:02:05.391
The question is just how quickly

00:02:05.391 --> 00:02:07.727
when they will be usable here in Ukraine

00:02:07.994 --> 00:02:09.395
and what happens

00:02:09.395 --> 00:02:10.630
in the meantime, specifically

00:02:10.630 --> 00:02:11.731
for those soldiers

00:02:11.731 --> 00:02:12.932
who are very bravely trying

00:02:12.932 --> 00:02:15.602
to hold out against increasing

00:02:15.602 --> 00:02:16.836
increasingly determined

00:02:16.836 --> 00:02:18.571
and numerous Russian troops.

00:02:18.571 --> 00:02:20.807
John Sabel live for us in Kiev.

00:02:20.807 --> 00:02:21.841
Melissa, thank you so much.

00:02:21.841 --> 00:02:23.510
Let's get some perspective now from the

00:02:23.510 --> 00:02:25.044
lieutenant general, Mark Hertling.

00:02:25.044 --> 00:02:27.113
He said served as commanding general,

00:02:27.113 --> 00:02:27.480
the U.S.

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:28.047
Army, Europe

00:02:28.047 --> 00:02:29.849
and the Seventh Army general.

00:02:29.849 --> 00:02:30.884
Grateful for your time,

00:02:30.884 --> 00:02:32.018
especially on this day.

00:02:32.018 --> 00:02:34.020
You just heard Melissa explain

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:35.288
what we're hearing from soldiers

00:02:35.288 --> 00:02:35.822
on the ground

00:02:35.822 --> 00:02:36.990
President Zelensky himself

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:38.625
calls it challenging.

00:02:38.625 --> 00:02:39.726
If I could ask the controller

00:02:39.726 --> 00:02:40.693
to put the map back up.

00:02:40.693 --> 00:02:42.061
When you look at back mood

00:02:42.061 --> 00:02:44.397
and where it is in southeastern Ukraine,

00:02:44.397 --> 00:02:45.865
if you're in the room trying to debate

00:02:45.865 --> 00:02:47.433
military strategy here.

00:02:47.433 --> 00:02:48.401
Is it

00:02:48.601 --> 00:02:50.403
smart maybe to give it up

00:02:50.403 --> 00:02:52.105
and then come back and fight another day

00:02:52.105 --> 00:02:54.407
or is holding it of some strategic

00:02:54.407 --> 00:02:56.309
whether it's strategic on the battlefield

00:02:56.309 --> 00:02:57.177
or strategic

00:02:57.177 --> 00:02:58.811
in terms of public opinion,

00:02:58.811 --> 00:03:00.380
public morale, to keep it

00:03:02.382 --> 00:03:03.349
Yes, John.

00:03:03.349 --> 00:03:04.250
All of the above.

00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:05.552
What we're talking about

00:03:05.552 --> 00:03:07.787
is an inconsequential city.

00:03:08.154 --> 00:03:08.922
Before the war,

00:03:08.922 --> 00:03:11.391
it was a population of about 70,000.

00:03:11.424 --> 00:03:12.959
It's a small

00:03:12.959 --> 00:03:15.662
area, small city on the intersection

00:03:15.662 --> 00:03:16.596
of a couple of roads

00:03:16.596 --> 00:03:18.731
and near some railroads for resupply.

00:03:18.998 --> 00:03:21.167
It is not strategically important,

00:03:21.467 --> 00:03:23.036
but it has become

00:03:23.036 --> 00:03:24.604
strategically imperative

00:03:24.604 --> 00:03:26.673
to hold by the Ukrainians

00:03:26.673 --> 00:03:28.741
and certainly by the Russians

00:03:28.741 --> 00:03:29.709
trying to take it.

00:03:29.709 --> 00:03:31.711
I would equate this somewhat

00:03:31.711 --> 00:03:34.047
like Bastogne during World War Two,

00:03:34.047 --> 00:03:35.348
the Battle of the Bulge,

00:03:35.348 --> 00:03:37.517
the city itself was not critical,

00:03:37.517 --> 00:03:39.018
but holding on to it.

00:03:39.018 --> 00:03:39.752
The Ukrainians

00:03:39.752 --> 00:03:41.821
saying we are not going to give this up.

00:03:42.021 --> 00:03:42.989
We're going to suck

00:03:42.989 --> 00:03:45.091
a whole lot more Russians into this

00:03:45.091 --> 00:03:46.593
into this malaise

00:03:46.593 --> 00:03:48.895
and cause more problems is important

00:03:49.162 --> 00:03:50.496
to them, certainly.

00:03:50.496 --> 00:03:51.931
And the Russians need a victory

00:03:51.931 --> 00:03:53.967
that they have not been able to achieve.

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:54.434
John,

00:03:54.434 --> 00:03:56.135
how long have we been talking about

00:03:56.135 --> 00:03:57.170
the city of back move?

00:03:57.170 --> 00:03:58.871
It's been months now

00:03:58.871 --> 00:04:00.373
and the Ukrainians continue

00:04:00.373 --> 00:04:01.708
to hold on to it.

00:04:01.708 --> 00:04:03.243
And so in that context,

00:04:03.243 --> 00:04:05.044
you talk about Putin could use a win,

00:04:06.179 --> 00:04:07.680
even if it's a small one.

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:09.215
When you hear it's quite obvious

00:04:09.215 --> 00:04:10.216
that Russia has suffered

00:04:10.216 --> 00:04:11.718
huge losses on the battlefield

00:04:11.718 --> 00:04:12.652
over the last year.

00:04:12.652 --> 00:04:13.753
Now we're into the first month

00:04:13.753 --> 00:04:15.288
of the second year of this war.

00:04:15.288 --> 00:04:15.822
Yet to hear

00:04:15.822 --> 00:04:16.489
Putin say it

00:04:16.489 --> 00:04:18.491
so publicly acknowledging,

00:04:18.491 --> 00:04:20.126
what does that tell you?

00:04:20.126 --> 00:04:21.427
Who's that aimed for in your view?

00:04:21.427 --> 00:04:22.595
Is it aimed at trying to keep up

00:04:22.595 --> 00:04:23.763
military morale, saying,

00:04:23.763 --> 00:04:24.364
I hear it,

00:04:24.364 --> 00:04:25.231
I understand

00:04:25.231 --> 00:04:25.832
you're hurting

00:04:25.832 --> 00:04:26.666
and some of your families

00:04:26.666 --> 00:04:27.600
have suffered profoundly?

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:28.635
Is it about public opinion?

00:04:28.635 --> 00:04:29.969
All of the above

00:04:31.104 --> 00:04:32.905
Well, it's all of the above also.

00:04:32.905 --> 00:04:33.606
But but here's

00:04:33.606 --> 00:04:35.942
the context of Putin's speech today.

00:04:36.342 --> 00:04:36.709
Today,

00:04:36.709 --> 00:04:38.645
he was talking to the FSB,

00:04:38.645 --> 00:04:40.747
which is the organization

00:04:40.847 --> 00:04:42.649
that followed on to the KGB,

00:04:42.649 --> 00:04:44.817
some a group that he was once a part of.

00:04:45.151 --> 00:04:47.053
So when he was talking about casualties

00:04:47.053 --> 00:04:49.255
was just one part of that speech.

00:04:49.255 --> 00:04:51.691
He was also telling the FBI, FSB

00:04:51.958 --> 00:04:53.626
increased the

00:04:54.661 --> 00:04:55.795
supervision and

00:04:55.795 --> 00:04:58.064
oversight of the Russian population.

00:04:58.264 --> 00:05:00.600
And he was doing this on a day

00:05:00.767 --> 00:05:03.269
when Ukrainian drones were flying over

00:05:03.269 --> 00:05:04.904
Russian cities, by my account,

00:05:04.904 --> 00:05:06.172
12 different cities.

00:05:06.172 --> 00:05:08.675
A few days after there was a successful

00:05:08.841 --> 00:05:10.143
Ukrainian Russians

00:05:10.143 --> 00:05:11.544
strike against that Russian

00:05:11.544 --> 00:05:13.746
air AWACS plane in Belarus.

00:05:13.746 --> 00:05:16.115
And and the fact of the matter is

00:05:16.115 --> 00:05:17.050
that he's saying

00:05:17.050 --> 00:05:18.685
Putin is seeing more

00:05:18.685 --> 00:05:19.986
and more

00:05:20.286 --> 00:05:22.689
demonstrations against what's happening,

00:05:22.855 --> 00:05:24.357
and that's going to increase

00:05:24.357 --> 00:05:25.692
as more and more dead

00:05:25.692 --> 00:05:27.927
bodies come home to Russian mothers.

00:05:27.927 --> 00:05:30.363
So what Putin is basically saying today

00:05:30.363 --> 00:05:30.763
is, yeah,

00:05:30.763 --> 00:05:32.732
we're having problems on the battlefield

00:05:32.732 --> 00:05:35.401
and he's telling the FSB, increase

00:05:35.702 --> 00:05:38.037
the things you're doing to put down

00:05:38.938 --> 00:05:40.306
the Russian population,

00:05:40.306 --> 00:05:41.574
the Russian citizens.

00:05:41.574 --> 00:05:43.643
So it is not a good sign for Mr.

00:05:43.643 --> 00:05:45.345
Putin today, in my view.

00:05:45.345 --> 00:05:47.480
He's having some problems back home.

00:05:47.480 --> 00:05:48.581
General Hertling, as always, sir,

00:05:48.581 --> 00:05:49.749
thank you for your time.

00:05:49.749 --> 00:05:51.884
Vladimir Putin delivered a major speech

00:05:51.884 --> 00:05:54.053
a short time ago to the FSB.

00:05:54.053 --> 00:05:55.188
That is Russia's

00:05:55.188 --> 00:05:56.889
Federal Security Service.

00:05:56.889 --> 00:05:59.192
Putin admitted that members of the FSB

00:05:59.192 --> 00:06:00.993
have actually been killed in Ukraine,

00:06:00.993 --> 00:06:03.096
and he urged the intelligence agency

00:06:03.296 --> 00:06:04.831
to step up its work to counter

00:06:04.831 --> 00:06:06.632
Western spy agencies.

00:06:06.632 --> 00:06:07.200
That speech

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:09.535
comes as intense fighting continues

00:06:09.736 --> 00:06:11.003
around the town of Buck

00:06:11.003 --> 00:06:12.038
in eastern Ukraine.

00:06:18.478 --> 00:06:19.812
Ukrainian forces say that

00:06:19.812 --> 00:06:21.781
the situation is getting dire

00:06:21.781 --> 00:06:24.150
and they are running out of ammunition

00:06:24.150 --> 00:06:25.718
Let's bring in Steve Hall.

00:06:25.718 --> 00:06:27.487
He's a national security analyst

00:06:27.487 --> 00:06:27.787
and a

00:06:27.787 --> 00:06:31.023
former CIA chief of Russia operations.

00:06:31.591 --> 00:06:32.258
So, Steve,

00:06:32.258 --> 00:06:32.859
I wonder,

00:06:32.859 --> 00:06:34.327
what was your takeaway

00:06:34.327 --> 00:06:36.662
from Putin's speech this morning?

00:06:36.662 --> 00:06:39.065
Was the point here to kind of rally

00:06:39.065 --> 00:06:39.565
the troops

00:06:39.565 --> 00:06:43.136
at a really tough moment in this war?

00:06:43.803 --> 00:06:44.937
Yes, certainly that's part of it.

00:06:44.937 --> 00:06:46.105
I mean, I think there's a lot going on

00:06:46.105 --> 00:06:46.906
in the speech, a lot

00:06:46.906 --> 00:06:48.775
that Putin wanted to try to accomplish.

00:06:48.775 --> 00:06:49.675
First and foremost

00:06:49.675 --> 00:06:51.844
was to try to increase the morale

00:06:51.844 --> 00:06:53.579
inside the FSB

00:06:53.579 --> 00:06:55.248
the one of the major security services,

00:06:55.248 --> 00:06:57.116
probably the strongest in Russia.

00:06:57.116 --> 00:06:59.285
They do have folks on on the ground

00:06:59.285 --> 00:07:00.453
in Ukraine,

00:07:00.453 --> 00:07:01.320
like many intelligence

00:07:01.320 --> 00:07:03.122
services, security services.

00:07:03.122 --> 00:07:03.956
They had a wartime

00:07:03.956 --> 00:07:05.391
sort of paramilitary capability,

00:07:05.391 --> 00:07:06.092
both collection

00:07:06.092 --> 00:07:08.861
and also to conduct attacks and so forth.

00:07:09.328 --> 00:07:10.563
But as Putin alluded to,

00:07:10.563 --> 00:07:11.397
they also have a very,

00:07:11.397 --> 00:07:12.131
very important role

00:07:12.131 --> 00:07:12.965
that they need to continue

00:07:12.965 --> 00:07:14.133
playing inside of Russia.

00:07:14.133 --> 00:07:16.502
And that's the counterintelligence piece

00:07:16.502 --> 00:07:17.737
that he mentioned several times in

00:07:17.737 --> 00:07:18.204
the speech.

00:07:19.172 --> 00:07:20.740
And he also urged the FSB

00:07:20.740 --> 00:07:22.442
to step up their operations

00:07:22.442 --> 00:07:23.509
to counteract

00:07:23.509 --> 00:07:25.511
Western intelligence services,

00:07:25.511 --> 00:07:27.980
who he says has boosted their operations.

00:07:27.980 --> 00:07:30.082
So I wonder, I mean, should the West,

00:07:30.082 --> 00:07:30.883
the US

00:07:30.883 --> 00:07:32.718
and NATO's nations be concerned

00:07:32.718 --> 00:07:33.586
about what this means

00:07:33.586 --> 00:07:35.521
for them in the near term?

00:07:36.622 --> 00:07:39.058
I don't think it's a real change.

00:07:39.058 --> 00:07:40.259
These things are sort of going on

00:07:40.259 --> 00:07:40.860
in the background

00:07:40.860 --> 00:07:42.595
and Putin mentioned them in his speech,

00:07:42.595 --> 00:07:43.062
but at all, it's

00:07:43.062 --> 00:07:45.465
one big ball of of responsibilities

00:07:45.465 --> 00:07:47.233
that the FSB had inside of Russia.

00:07:47.233 --> 00:07:47.867
So when he

00:07:47.867 --> 00:07:48.301
when putting out

00:07:48.301 --> 00:07:49.836
first of counterintelligence, he's

00:07:49.836 --> 00:07:51.204
not just talking about

00:07:51.204 --> 00:07:53.439
the work of Western intelligence services

00:07:53.439 --> 00:07:55.007
and other intelligence services,

00:07:55.007 --> 00:07:56.342
although that's part of it.

00:07:56.342 --> 00:07:57.810
What he's really concerned about

00:07:57.810 --> 00:07:59.545
is dissidents inside of Russia.

00:07:59.545 --> 00:08:01.180
And there's an entire center

00:08:01.180 --> 00:08:02.281
inside the FSB

00:08:02.281 --> 00:08:03.316
that is responsible

00:08:03.316 --> 00:08:04.484
for not only monitoring,

00:08:04.484 --> 00:08:05.485
but also

00:08:05.485 --> 00:08:07.053
taking care of eliminating

00:08:07.053 --> 00:08:07.820
or as the Russians say

00:08:07.820 --> 00:08:09.455
it, liquidating dissidents.

00:08:09.455 --> 00:08:10.923
And he's very, very concerned,

00:08:10.923 --> 00:08:11.891
I think, about that

00:08:11.891 --> 00:08:13.826
because of how poorly the war is going.

00:08:13.826 --> 00:08:14.760
He's got to monitor it

00:08:14.760 --> 00:08:16.162
very, very carefully.

00:08:16.162 --> 00:08:16.429
Yeah.

00:08:16.429 --> 00:08:18.431
And they're taking a lot of casualties,

00:08:18.431 --> 00:08:20.900
those casualties going back to Russia.

00:08:21.367 --> 00:08:22.802
What effect all that will have?

00:08:22.802 --> 00:08:24.003
I think we are definitely all

00:08:24.003 --> 00:08:24.971
looking to see.

